&lt;p&gt;Open Data Platform by OpenBB (ODP) is the open-source toolset that helps data engineers integrate proprietary, licensed, and public data sources into downstream applications like AI copilots and research dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ODP operates as the &amp;ldquo;connect once, consume everywhere&amp;rdquo; infrastructure layer that consolidates and exposes data to multiple surfaces at once: Python environments for quants, OpenBB Workspace and Excel for analysts, MCP servers for AI agents, and REST APIs for other applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;a href=&#34;https://pro.openbb.co&#34;&gt;
  &lt;div align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://openbb-cms.directus.app/assets/70b971ef-7a7e-486e-b5ae-1cc602f2162c.png&#34; alt=&#34;Logo&#34; width=&#34;1000&#34;&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get started with: &lt;code&gt;pip install openbb&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nn&#34;&gt;openbb&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;kn&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;obb&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;output&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;obb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;historical&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;AAPL&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;df&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;output&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;to_dataframe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Data integrations available can be found here: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.openbb.co/python/reference&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://docs.openbb.co/python/reference&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;openbb-workspace&#34;&gt;OpenBB Workspace
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;While the Open Data Platform provides the open-source data integration foundation, &lt;strong&gt;OpenBB Workspace&lt;/strong&gt; offers the enterprise UI for analysts to visualize datasets and leverage AI agents. The platform&amp;rsquo;s &amp;ldquo;connect once, consume everywhere&amp;rdquo; architecture enables seamless integration between the two.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can find OpenBB Workspace at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://pro.openbb.co&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://pro.openbb.co&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;a href=&#34;https://pro.openbb.co&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;div align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://openbb-cms.directus.app/assets/f69b6aaf-0821-4bc8-a43c-715e03a924ef.png&#34; alt=&#34;Logo&#34; width=&#34;1000&#34;&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data integration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can learn more about adding data to the OpenBB workspace from the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.openbb.co/workspace&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;docs&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/OpenBB-finance/backends-for-openbb&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;this open source repository&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI Agents integration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can learn more about adding AI agents to the OpenBB workspace from &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/OpenBB-finance/agents-for-openbb&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;this open source repository&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;integrating-open-data-platform-to-the-openbb-workspace&#34;&gt;Integrating Open Data Platform to the OpenBB Workspace
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Connect this library to the OpenBB Workspace with a few simple commands, in a Python (3.9.21 - 3.12) environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;run-an-odp-backend&#34;&gt;Run an ODP backend
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install the packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;pip install &lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;openbb[all]&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start the API server over localhost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;openbb-api
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This will launch a FastAPI server, via Uvicorn, at &lt;code&gt;127.0.0.1:6900&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can check that it works by going to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://127.0.0.1:6900&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://127.0.0.1:6900&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;integrate-the-odp-backend-to-openbb-workspace&#34;&gt;Integrate the ODP Backend to OpenBB Workspace
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sign-in to the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://pro.openbb.co/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;OpenBB Workspace&lt;/a&gt;, and follow the following steps:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75cffb4a-5e95-470a-b9d0-6ffd4067e069&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;CleanShot 2025-05-17 at 09 51 56@2x&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go to the &amp;ldquo;Apps&amp;rdquo; tab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click on &amp;ldquo;Connect backend&amp;rdquo;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fill in the form with:
Name: Open Data Platform
URL: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://127.0.0.1:6900&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://127.0.0.1:6900&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click on &amp;ldquo;Test&amp;rdquo;. You should get a &amp;ldquo;Test successful&amp;rdquo; with the number of apps found.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click on &amp;ldquo;Add&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&amp;rsquo;s it.&lt;/p&gt;
